WEBVTT

00:02.060 --> 00:03.660
A long, long time ago.

00:03.870 --> 00:06.610
A story from about a hundred years ago.

00:07.680 --> 00:12.340
Nadja, guided by
destiny, arrived in France.

00:16.640 --> 00:17.440
- NAAJA
- Nadja,

00:18.000 --> 00:19.270
With your eyes

00:19.271 --> 00:20.539
Kimi no hitomi ni wa

00:20.540 --> 00:21.750
- Nadja,
- NAAJA

00:21.753 --> 00:22.880
What do you see?

00:22.881 --> 00:24.010
Nani ga mieru

00:24.210 --> 00:25.650
Shining in the far distance,

00:25.651 --> 00:27.090
Haruka tooku hikaru

00:27.220 --> 00:28.325
The door to the future,

00:28.326 --> 00:29.430
Mirai no tobira

00:30.320 --> 00:31.940
That's what I'm searching for

00:31.941 --> 00:33.560
Sagashite iru

00:33.590 --> 00:37.280
Tomorrow's Nadja

00:41.660 --> 00:43.540
If everyone could meet with a smile

00:43.541 --> 00:45.420
Minna egao de aetara

00:45.540 --> 00:48.790
- I'm sure there would be no more fighting
- Arasoi mo kitto nakunaru

00:48.920 --> 00:50.525
It could be so much more fun

00:50.526 --> 00:52.130
Konna ni mo tanoshi kunaru

00:52.210 --> 00:53.920
The world is wide, but it's still one

00:53.921 --> 00:55.630
Sekai wa hiroi kedo hitotsu ne

00:56.050 --> 00:57.700
I can't see the end of the journey

00:57.701 --> 00:59.350
Tabi no owari wa mienai

00:59.390 --> 01:02.720
- God is the only one who could
possibly know - Kamisama ga tabun shitteru

01:02.850 --> 01:06.440
- To the people who, someday, I will meet
again - Itsukamata deaeru hito tachi ni

01:06.443 --> 01:07.500
I will go waving

01:07.501 --> 01:08.560
Te wo furinagara

01:08.860 --> 01:12.175
Sometimes, there are days I feel blue,

01:12.176 --> 01:15.489
Toki ni wa BURUU ni naru hi mo aru kedo

01:15.490 --> 01:16.845
But I won't look back

01:16.846 --> 01:18.200
Ushiro mukanai

01:18.450 --> 01:20.930
Until the day my dream comes true

01:20.931 --> 01:23.410
Yume ga kanau hi made

01:23.660 --> 01:25.370
Nadja, Your smile

01:25.371 --> 01:27.079
NAAJA kimi no hohoemi wa

01:27.080 --> 01:28.750
Nadja, gives me courage

01:28.751 --> 01:30.420
NAAJA yuuki ni naru

01:30.630 --> 01:32.090
Under the blue sky,

01:32.091 --> 01:33.549
Aoi sora no shita de

01:33.550 --> 01:34.965
I will find the place

01:34.966 --> 01:36.380
Ashita no yukue

01:36.970 --> 01:38.785
where my future lies

01:38.786 --> 01:40.600
Mitsukeru kara

01:52.220 --> 01:53.220
Dear Mother.

01:53.920 --> 01:58.460
After I left the Applefield Orphanage,
I joined the Dandelion Troupe.

01:59.600 --> 02:00.840
It was my first time in London.

02:01.580 --> 02:02.880
My very first dance performance.

02:03.360 --> 02:05.540
And my very first ball.

02:06.520 --> 02:10.280
The night that I wore your dress
and danced with the star-eyed knight –

02:10.860 --> 02:13.180
I'll surely never forget it.

02:14.400 --> 02:17.040
And then, I left England.

02:17.300 --> 02:19.720
I'm now heading for Paris, France.

02:30.720 --> 02:32.000
This is...

02:32.300 --> 02:34.160
The Eiffel Tower is visible now!

02:34.410 --> 02:35.900
Oh? Really?

02:44.780 --> 02:46.720
Hello, France.

02:46.840 --> 02:48.380
Bonjour, Paris!

02:55.040 --> 02:58.420
The Diary of the Ball that
Ties Mother and Daughter

03:11.800 --> 03:13.190
All right, folks!

03:13.740 --> 03:16.900
Next up, is the new face
in our Dandelion Troupe:

03:17.080 --> 03:18.200
Nadja!

03:18.740 --> 03:20.600
The blue fairy that dances in Paris.

03:20.740 --> 03:23.540
Please look forward to
Nadja's glorious dance!

04:18.260 --> 04:19.280
Very nice.

04:30.240 --> 04:33.200
Hi! You over there, Miss Platinum-blonde!

04:36.420 --> 04:38.120
My name's T.J.

04:38.360 --> 04:39.360
What's your name?

04:39.960 --> 04:40.960
Nadja.

04:41.440 --> 04:43.200
Nadja Applefield.

04:44.570 --> 04:46.580
Nadja? Nadja, huh?

04:46.850 --> 04:47.850
That's nice!

04:52.510 --> 04:53.566
Pleased to meet you, Nadja.

04:53.590 --> 04:56.320
To be honest, you're my type.

04:56.930 --> 04:58.200
Is this your first time in Paris?

04:58.201 --> 04:59.320
Let go of that hand!

05:01.050 --> 05:02.460
Get away from Nadja!

05:02.880 --> 05:04.780
What are you to Nadja?

05:05.030 --> 05:06.910
"What am I?" I'm...

05:07.930 --> 05:09.030
What am I?

05:09.540 --> 05:11.750
In short, not her boyfriend.

05:12.010 --> 05:13.200
I-Idiot!

05:13.300 --> 05:14.540
I didn't mean–!

05:14.690 --> 05:16.200
If that's the case, stay out of this.

05:16.380 --> 05:18.670
You have no right to get
in the way of my romance.

05:18.750 --> 05:19.870
What?!

05:20.760 --> 05:22.420
Let's get away from this guy, shall we?

05:22.710 --> 05:24.460
I'll show you the streets of Paris.

05:24.540 --> 05:25.540
Wait a minute!

05:26.620 --> 05:28.800
You're pretty brave to insult a samurai.

05:29.000 --> 05:30.220
Take your stance!

05:30.400 --> 05:32.150
I challenge you to a fair fight!

05:32.970 --> 05:34.700
A challenge? Fine.

05:35.230 --> 05:37.120
Wait a minute you two!

05:39.270 --> 05:40.870
Hey, come on!

05:41.130 --> 05:42.920
W-What the heck is that stance?

05:43.770 --> 05:44.980
Don't you know?

05:45.430 --> 05:48.140
It's America's national sport, baseball.

05:48.190 --> 05:49.940
Well, anywhere is fine.

05:50.050 --> 05:51.540
Throw your pitch!

05:56.210 --> 05:57.920
I don't know baseball or whatever that is,

05:58.160 --> 06:01.160
But, using a samurai's soul for
something like that is unforgivable!

06:01.330 --> 06:02.780
Something like that?

06:02.840 --> 06:06.100
What do you mean by calling
America's soul "something like that"?

06:06.300 --> 06:08.600
Now, now. Calm down you two.

06:08.680 --> 06:10.220
Nadja, stay out of this!

06:11.030 --> 06:12.360
I'll warn you now, I'm strong!

06:12.460 --> 06:14.460
What?! Aren't you being
a little full of yourself?

06:14.740 --> 06:15.740
What about you?

06:20.910 --> 06:22.380
Ah-choo!

06:30.020 --> 06:31.040
T-Thanks.

06:33.460 --> 06:36.820
Hey, it's your fault that Nadja got angry.

06:37.040 --> 06:38.040
What did you say?!

06:38.120 --> 06:40.370
It's because you told
her to "stay out of this!"

06:40.470 --> 06:41.700
You too! How can you–

06:41.701 --> 06:42.960
Ahem, ahem.

06:49.720 --> 06:50.890
Bitter isn't it?

06:51.030 --> 06:52.060
Parisian tea that is.

06:52.100 --> 06:53.680
It's a question of how you make it.

06:53.910 --> 06:55.300
Parisian tea is bitter.

06:55.600 --> 06:57.000
Parisian water is cold.

06:57.380 --> 06:59.180
Parisian kids are snotty.

06:59.980 --> 07:02.080
Stop with this "Paris, Paris" stuff!

07:02.580 --> 07:03.580
Paris...

07:04.800 --> 07:06.700
That's right! That's it!

07:06.930 --> 07:08.240
Ah! She spoke!

07:10.160 --> 07:12.550
You two, take a look at this.

07:13.450 --> 07:14.510
What is this?

07:15.080 --> 07:16.600
It's my mother's diary.

07:17.030 --> 07:18.940
I can't read the foreign words,

07:19.230 --> 07:21.140
but I did recognize the word "Paris."

07:21.590 --> 07:22.590
It's true.

07:23.020 --> 07:24.890
But, what about it?

07:25.670 --> 07:29.460
Nadja was raised in an
orphanage all of her life.

07:29.730 --> 07:32.400
But recently, she's found
out that her mother is still alive.

07:33.740 --> 07:36.660
That's why I'm looking for my mother.

07:37.640 --> 07:40.180
I want to meet her, even
if it's just to look at her.

07:40.810 --> 07:43.020
I see, so that's why.

07:43.650 --> 07:45.820
If that's the case, you
should leave it to me!

07:47.060 --> 07:50.120
After all, I'm the investigative
reporter Harvey Livingston's brother,

07:50.710 --> 07:52.840
T.J. Livingston!

07:53.330 --> 07:54.510
His brother?!

07:58.520 --> 08:01.060
Harvey, stop sleeping! Work, work!

08:03.580 --> 08:05.060
What a surprise...

08:05.390 --> 08:07.760
You're <i>that</i> Harvey's brother.

08:08.220 --> 08:11.560
Harvey's over in London,
so why are you in Paris, T.J.?

08:12.110 --> 08:16.240
Harvey works for the Montartre
Journal's main office in Paris,

08:16.620 --> 08:19.440
but right now he's in London,
chasing the Black Rose.

08:19.830 --> 08:24.050
To tell you the truth, I wanted
to go with him, but I have school.

08:24.820 --> 08:27.240
Harvey is a superman who can do anything!

08:27.860 --> 08:30.880
I want to hurry and
grow up to be like Harvey!

08:31.540 --> 08:32.540
That's why,

08:32.710 --> 08:36.200
you should leave everything here
to the future investigative reporter.

08:44.060 --> 08:46.320
Does anyone know how to read these words?

08:48.920 --> 08:50.560
Uh. Let's see, let's see.

08:52.600 --> 08:53.600
Abel.

08:53.990 --> 08:56.160
Oh, this is German.

08:57.630 --> 08:59.600
"Ah, Paris at long last."

09:00.110 --> 09:01.740
"My first ball."

09:01.940 --> 09:05.580
"My first dance partner
was a painter from Paris,"

09:05.860 --> 09:07.880
"Alphonse Jean Maley."

09:08.270 --> 09:10.540
"We danced the waltz together."

09:11.200 --> 09:14.200
"His paintings show
people who are so full of life."

09:14.340 --> 09:17.030
"It's as if they might move at any moment."

09:17.910 --> 09:20.700
It looks like this is the diary of a ball.

09:21.510 --> 09:23.430
Diary? Of a ball?

09:23.810 --> 09:27.760
When a girl goes to a ball, they log
their impressions of dance partners,

09:27.910 --> 09:31.800
or names and descriptions of the
gentlemen they expect to dance with.

09:32.390 --> 09:33.480
Oh?

09:34.260 --> 09:36.150
Thank you, Abel!

09:37.920 --> 09:39.460
Nadja, where are you going?

09:39.520 --> 09:41.450
Isn't it obvious? To look for him!

09:41.900 --> 09:43.990
Eh? That painter?

09:44.330 --> 09:45.330
That's right.

09:45.400 --> 09:47.560
He might know something
about my mother, right?

09:48.100 --> 09:49.720
But, in the middle of Paris?

09:49.760 --> 09:50.760
Let's go look!

09:50.930 --> 09:51.930
I'll help too.

09:52.460 --> 09:53.480
Kennosuke!

09:53.790 --> 09:55.080
The Tsurugi family motto:

09:55.280 --> 09:58.360
"You will achieve it if you try. But
nothing will be achieved if you do not."

09:59.000 --> 10:01.320
It means that if you want
to, you can do anything!

10:02.090 --> 10:03.180
Thank you!

10:04.230 --> 10:06.080
Hmph! Family motto? Talk about out-of-date.

10:06.430 --> 10:07.800
Did you say something?

10:08.100 --> 10:09.470
Beats me.

10:11.360 --> 10:12.360
Hmph!

10:14.860 --> 10:16.260
Anyway, where do we look?

10:16.890 --> 10:17.890
I don't know...

10:18.290 --> 10:19.960
But, at any rate, we should look.

10:20.000 --> 10:22.260
It's futile to search blindly.

10:22.420 --> 10:23.840
Well, what do you suggest?

10:24.110 --> 10:26.880
To start, we can go to shops that sell art.

10:27.110 --> 10:29.820
Then, find out if anyone there
knows a painter named Maley.

10:29.880 --> 10:30.880
I see!

10:31.050 --> 10:32.860
As expected from the
investigative reporter!

10:40.330 --> 10:41.430
Geez.

10:41.630 --> 10:43.400
Treating me like a kid.

10:43.590 --> 10:45.350
"As expected of the
investigative reporter."

10:45.710 --> 10:48.090
Well? Where do we look next?

10:49.240 --> 10:53.060
I don't want to be asked that by a
guy who just looks stupid and follows.

10:53.420 --> 10:54.420
What?!

10:54.570 --> 10:55.570
That's enough!

10:55.610 --> 10:57.570
You want to have water dumped on you again?

10:58.070 --> 10:59.400
We get it.

11:00.490 --> 11:01.670
Good boys.

11:04.240 --> 11:05.490
Huh?

11:07.150 --> 11:08.150
Mama...

11:09.130 --> 11:10.380
Could it be...

11:10.910 --> 11:12.080
you're lost?

11:34.930 --> 11:37.220
I see, you're called Madeleine.

11:37.980 --> 11:40.230
I'm Nadja, pleased to meet you.

11:40.580 --> 11:42.340
Yup, Nadja.

11:43.380 --> 11:45.560
Geez, Nadja is such a Good Samaritan.

11:45.830 --> 11:47.800
I thought we were looking for that painter.

11:48.670 --> 11:50.180
It can't be helped, right?

11:50.240 --> 11:52.080
In a situation like that.

11:52.660 --> 11:53.880
What's more,

11:54.510 --> 11:55.940
She wants to see her mother.

11:56.390 --> 11:58.100
That girl felt the same way.

11:58.220 --> 12:00.140
Nadja couldn't leave her.

12:04.020 --> 12:05.020
Hey!

12:07.270 --> 12:09.660
I'm Kennosuke. Nice to meet you!

12:11.640 --> 12:12.640
Yup.

13:26.720 --> 13:28.040
Say, Madeleine.

13:28.140 --> 13:28.680
Huh?

13:28.980 --> 13:31.020
Do you really remember nothing?

13:31.360 --> 13:35.780
Like your mother's name, or where
she lives, or where you went astray?

13:36.160 --> 13:38.240
It could be anything. Try to remember.

13:39.550 --> 13:40.420
I don't know.

13:40.421 --> 13:41.520
That doesn't cut it!

13:42.030 --> 13:44.430
Stop and really try to remember.

13:45.710 --> 13:48.220
If you think that someone
will rescue you every time...

13:48.300 --> 13:49.480
You're sadly mistaken!

13:49.720 --> 13:52.040
What'll happen if you
don't pull yourself together?!

13:52.190 --> 13:53.190
Stop that!

13:55.080 --> 13:56.220
What the heck?!

13:56.520 --> 13:59.900
Blaming the child like that,
what will it resolve?

13:59.960 --> 14:01.880
You're being too easy on her.

14:01.950 --> 14:04.120
That's not helping her at all!

14:04.330 --> 14:05.040
Hmph.

14:05.180 --> 14:07.000
Some investigative reporter you are.

14:07.040 --> 14:08.040
What?!

14:08.150 --> 14:11.040
I used to think that your
brother was awesome.

14:11.510 --> 14:13.360
But the way his little brother acts...

14:13.400 --> 14:15.700
I guess your brother's
not so great after all.

14:17.080 --> 14:18.080
Take it back.

14:18.140 --> 14:19.140
Huh?

14:20.600 --> 14:23.360
I won't forgive anyone who insults Harvey.

14:24.000 --> 14:25.260
Take it back right now!

14:26.400 --> 14:27.400
No way.

14:27.840 --> 14:30.280
You don't understand how
a child in this situation feels.

14:30.560 --> 14:31.820
Who do you think you are?

14:32.070 --> 14:33.140
Take it back!

14:35.160 --> 14:37.020
What the hell do you know?!

14:37.140 --> 14:40.340
What me and Harvey had
to go through all this time!

14:40.380 --> 14:42.030
So what?

14:42.890 --> 14:45.900
You refuse to help someone
who's weaker than you.

14:46.020 --> 14:48.360
I can't believe anything you say!

14:48.580 --> 14:50.420
We should be protecting her!

14:50.480 --> 14:53.000
So you think being weak is okay?

14:53.100 --> 14:54.200
What did you say?!

14:54.560 --> 14:58.860
If she's weak, we should
help her become strong!

14:58.930 --> 15:00.340
Darn it! Both of you, stop!

15:00.390 --> 15:01.840
Nadja, stay out of this!

15:03.020 --> 15:04.090
I can't!

15:06.230 --> 15:07.760
You're both selfish!

15:07.980 --> 15:11.580
If you were really thinking about
her, you wouldn't be fighting!

15:12.600 --> 15:16.220
Don't you understand what
this child is feeling right now?

15:16.950 --> 15:19.160
All alone and in pain.

15:19.660 --> 15:22.160
Uncertainty and sadness.

15:22.800 --> 15:26.080
Why can't you understand
something so simple?

15:49.010 --> 15:50.480
This bell toll...

15:55.600 --> 16:00.760
Above the calm forest

16:01.170 --> 16:06.420
Shines a single star

16:06.730 --> 16:12.180
A love song plays

16:12.260 --> 16:17.700
Gentle is the wind in the farm

16:18.270 --> 16:22.900
Little birds and little goats

16:23.340 --> 16:28.220
In their mother's embrace

16:28.860 --> 16:34.280
Playing within a dream

16:34.400 --> 16:42.400
Blooming flowers in a fragrant garden

16:46.480 --> 16:51.620
Hold in the palm of your hand

16:47.180 --> 16:49.320
I have a little sister.

16:50.500 --> 16:53.200
My mother and father died 3 years ago.

16:53.201 --> 16:55.690
The smiles of this passing day's sun.

16:55.691 --> 16:58.280
I thought, "It's up to
me to protect Hanako."

16:58.281 --> 17:02.280
Good night, good night.

16:58.740 --> 16:59.740
Kennosuke...

17:00.240 --> 17:02.960
Right now, she's under
the care of relatives.

17:02.961 --> 17:10.660
As I hold you, my darling child.

17:03.400 --> 17:06.080
But someday, I'll go to Japan for her.

17:06.790 --> 17:08.160
That's why, I...

17:08.560 --> 17:10.580
It'd be nice if you could hurry to her.

17:10.950 --> 17:12.420
T.J...

17:12.980 --> 17:15.020
My parents died early too.

17:15.600 --> 17:21.100
He won't say it openly, but Harvey's
had plenty of hardships because of me.

17:23.020 --> 17:24.940
Nothing will happen
if you just keep crying.

17:25.230 --> 17:26.540
Isn't that right, T.J?

17:27.880 --> 17:31.480
It's all right since I'm here for you
now, but what would you do if I wasn't?

17:32.580 --> 17:34.540
Become strong, T.J.

17:36.890 --> 17:38.000
So, that's why.

17:38.390 --> 17:40.460
I have to become stronger.

17:41.130 --> 17:42.220
I'm sorry...

17:42.900 --> 17:45.320
I didn't know anything about you two.

17:45.880 --> 17:49.180
No, no, that's not what I wanted to say.

17:49.260 --> 17:52.560
Yup. I feel the same as Kennosuke.

17:52.920 --> 17:54.440
Nadja and Madeleine, both of you...

17:54.660 --> 17:56.660
I hope you will find your mothers.

17:57.330 --> 17:58.330
Yes!

18:06.590 --> 18:08.100
Ahh, you kids.

18:08.140 --> 18:09.140
Huh?

18:09.550 --> 18:10.550
Madeleine!

18:12.150 --> 18:13.170
Mama!

18:13.700 --> 18:15.120
Where were you?!

18:15.500 --> 18:16.700
I was so worried.

18:17.710 --> 18:18.620
Are you alright?

18:18.720 --> 18:20.640
Mama!

18:19.340 --> 18:20.780
You bad girl...

18:22.280 --> 18:23.280
I see.

18:23.690 --> 18:27.200
She got lost while her mother
was having a sketch done.

18:28.450 --> 18:31.560
That's why you
remembered that child's face.

18:34.200 --> 18:36.560
Well, it's getting late,
we'd better get back.

18:36.850 --> 18:37.850
Eh? But...

18:37.900 --> 18:38.900
Is it all right?

18:39.560 --> 18:41.870
If today is no good,
there's still tomorrow.

18:42.640 --> 18:45.100
If tomorrow's no good,
there's the day after tomorrow.

18:45.430 --> 18:46.430
That's right!

18:47.210 --> 18:49.240
Good bye then, we're going home.

18:49.500 --> 18:50.500
Yes.

18:53.030 --> 18:54.720
What a wonderful picture.

18:55.590 --> 18:57.260
It's as if they might move at any moment.

19:04.020 --> 19:05.189
Miss.

19:05.190 --> 19:06.190
Huh?

19:06.310 --> 19:10.640
Will you allow me to draw a picture of you?

19:11.580 --> 19:12.800
Yes, it would be my pleasure.

19:19.180 --> 19:23.280
A long time ago, I met
someone who looked just like you.

19:23.720 --> 19:24.720
Eh?

19:24.860 --> 19:28.800
<i>She</i> said the same thing
when she saw that picture.

19:31.540 --> 19:32.880
Long ago, you see,

19:33.000 --> 19:36.880
I would draw portraits of
the nobility to make money.

19:37.280 --> 19:40.200
I may not look like it, but I
was pretty popular back then.

19:40.610 --> 19:43.620
So I showed up at balls and other events.

19:44.890 --> 19:48.740
Just like that, I met <i>her</i> one day.

19:52.470 --> 19:53.720
My, is that so?

19:54.270 --> 19:56.800
You are an artist, right?

19:57.350 --> 20:00.960
Yes, I may not look it, but
I'm quite famous in Paris.

20:01.190 --> 20:03.360
Now that I think of it,
I've seen them before.

20:03.620 --> 20:05.240
The drawings you've done.

20:06.110 --> 20:07.580
I'm honored.

20:08.040 --> 20:10.060
It was truly wonderful, that drawing.

20:10.580 --> 20:12.980
The picture of the Monmartre family.

20:13.510 --> 20:16.040
It was as if they might move at any moment.

20:21.250 --> 20:23.620
With that one conversation,
I realized something.

20:24.080 --> 20:28.040
The drawings I had been
making until then were terrible.

20:28.600 --> 20:33.370
That picture, it was the
first one I did in Paris.

20:33.920 --> 20:38.340
Since then, I've stopped doing
jobs that were only for money

20:38.760 --> 20:41.880
and only drew the pictures
I wanted to, every day.

20:42.750 --> 20:45.340
Then, could it be...

20:46.270 --> 20:47.370
You're...

20:47.590 --> 20:50.100
You're Mr. Alphonse Jean Maley?

20:50.710 --> 20:54.030
Uh... yes... how do you know my name?

20:54.400 --> 20:55.740
Eeeeh?!

20:57.860 --> 21:00.160
I see, that person wrote about me...

21:01.200 --> 21:05.440
Yes, I looked for you
from this clue in the diary.

21:08.940 --> 21:11.860
Umm, well, about my mother...

21:12.570 --> 21:15.870
I'm sorry... I just danced
with her at a ball once.

21:16.270 --> 21:20.820
I don't know her name or where she lives.

21:21.780 --> 21:22.820
I see.

21:23.700 --> 21:25.320
But, I can say this much.

21:25.430 --> 21:26.430
Eh?

21:27.910 --> 21:32.240
Your mother had a very
charming laugh, just like yours.

21:44.450 --> 21:45.480
Mother.

21:46.300 --> 21:49.820
Today, I met a person you once danced with.

21:51.610 --> 21:52.610
Just a little...

21:53.220 --> 21:57.240
Only just a little bit, but I feel
that I've come closer to you.

21:58.810 --> 22:00.250
I feel that they day I will meet you

22:00.720 --> 22:02.480
has come just a bit closer as well, Mother.

22:14.490 --> 22:16.115
Paris is sunnier than London

22:16.116 --> 22:17.740
RONDON don yori haretara PARI

22:17.860 --> 22:20.950
- Carmen likes paella more than pasta
- CARUMEN men yori PAERIYA suki

22:21.370 --> 22:24.455
The Queen of Spades is a fickle person

22:24.456 --> 22:27.540
SUPEEDO no jou kimagure yasan

22:28.500 --> 22:29.740
- Indeed
- Kitto

22:32.500 --> 22:34.920
- It's not use worrying about it
- Nayan datte MUDA yo

22:35.500 --> 22:37.065
Que sera sera, sera Sera

22:37.066 --> 22:38.630
KE SERA SERA SERA SERA

22:38.890 --> 22:41.245
Tomorrow's going to
be whatever it was meant

22:41.246 --> 22:43.600
Ashita nante itsumo naru you ni

22:43.680 --> 22:45.060
- To be, to be
- Naru naru

22:45.390 --> 22:47.895
The tree fog won

22:47.896 --> 22:50.400
Sekai KAERU tobi KONKUURU

22:50.860 --> 22:52.820
The world frog-jumping contest

22:52.821 --> 22:54.780
Yuushou shita yo AMAGAERU

22:57.990 --> 23:01.075
Under the kitten's paw

23:01.076 --> 23:04.160
Koneko chan no ashi no ura wa

23:04.580 --> 23:07.665
Is the scent of the sun, right?

23:07.666 --> 23:10.750
Otentou sama no nioi dane

23:13.590 --> 23:15.255
Paris is sunnier than London

23:15.256 --> 23:16.920
RONDON don yori haretara PARI

23:17.010 --> 23:20.010
- Carmen likes paella more than pasta
- CARUMEN men yori PAERIYA suki

23:20.510 --> 23:23.700
It's not the time to hang around

23:23.701 --> 23:26.890
Michikusa shite iru baai ja nai ne

23:27.770 --> 23:30.020
Indeed, indeed

23:30.021 --> 23:32.270
Kitto kitto

23:40.580 --> 23:41.920
- Tomorrow's Nadja
- Tomorrow's Nadja

23:44.490 --> 23:48.360
In a scattering of rose petals, the phantom
thief, Black Rose, appeared once again.

23:48.830 --> 23:51.329
The many traps that are
waiting on the dance stage...

23:51.330 --> 23:53.870
The Black Rose is cornered,
and he takes an unexpected turn.

23:54.210 --> 23:56.790
At that moment, a
terrible duty falls upon me!

23:57.200 --> 23:59.800
What's more, a puzzling
dark shadow draws upon Rita.

24:00.960 --> 24:02.049
Tomorrow's Nadja:

24:02.050 --> 24:03.340
The Masquerade Ball's Trap.

24:03.770 --> 24:05.800
Now, the Door of Destiny opens.
